# Web (multi-threaded) build config — read by scripts/build-game.sh.
#
# Must use the STANDARD (non-Mono) editor: Godot 4's Mono/.NET editor cannot export to Web
# at all ("Exporting to Web is currently not supported in Godot 4 when using C#/.NET" —
# confirmed directly against this project's Mono editor). The project itself is pure
# GDScript, so the standard editor exports it with no loss of functionality.
#
# Threaded means SharedArrayBuffer, which means the page MUST be served with
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy/Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy headers or the browser silently
# refuses threads — see scripts/serve-web-build.py, which sends both.

GODOT_BIN="godot/Godot_v4.7-stable_linux.x86_64"
PRESET_NAME="Web"
OUTPUT_DIR="builds/web-threaded"
OUTPUT_FILE="builds/web-threaded/index.html"
